{"type":"text","timestamp":1794558943215,"sessionID":"ses_e2bf9637cffehsWt94nfgLxMyQ","part":{"id":"prt_1d40c472c002zNlyzQHFuxfXhg","sessionID":"ses_e2bf9637cffehsWt94nfgLxMyQ","messageID":"msg_1d40c308e001B7AyvBF3CiOJ5X","type":"text","text":"T004 is complete. Both named files were modified, no other files touched, and the task checkbox was left unticked.\n\nFiles written:\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs` adds the pre-restore integrity pass in `restoreFromBackup`, with `assertWritable` on every recorded path and a sha256 comparison against each entry's recorded hash before any write. A mismatch prints `ERROR: the backup copy of <path> does not match its recorded hash, so nothing was restored. The backup is kept at <dir>` and returns `null`. The drop branch of `commandApply` now prints the \"could not be restored, so the tree is as the write left it\" line when that happens.\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/agents-md-embed.test.cjs` adds the failing-then-passing case on the `foreign` fixture. Its write hook damages the backup copy of `AGENTS.md` on the first call and then removes `- Never commit a generated file.` from the root document, as `dropALineOnWrite` does.\n\nVerify, before the source change (`node --test .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/agents-md-embed.test.cjs`):\n\n```\ntests 37\npass 36\nfail 1\n...\n✖ a damaged backup copy stops the restore and leaves the tree as the write left it\n  AssertionError: the mismatch is named with the backup it kept\n  [agents-md-embed] restored: 1 file(s) from .../doctor-agents-md/9dfb6bb99d9ed2e3\n  [agents-md-embed] the write dropped 1 line(s), so the run was undone; ...\n```\n\nVerify, after the change, same command:\n\n```\ntests 37\nsuites 0\npass 37\nfail 0\ncancelled 0\nskipped 0\ntodo 0\n```\n\n`node --check .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs` printed `SYNTAX_OK`. `git status --short` lists only the two named files as modified.\n\nOne implementation detail beyond the literal line: a missing backup copy is treated as the same mismatch failure, so the restore returns `null` instead of throwing on the read. Nothing was left undone and nothing is blocked on the operator.","time":{"start":1794558936876,"end":1794558943215}}}
